WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:01.000 --> 00:03.490
Hi Jerry, how are you fitting into your new role?

2
00:03.970 --> 00:06.340
Hi Linda. The work has been very exciting.

3
00:06.730 --> 00:10.980
Unfortunately, I'm having difficulty connecting
with my coworkers and new manager.

4
00:11.430 --> 00:13.190
Oh no! What's the problem?

5
00:13.770 --> 00:18.690
I don't know how I'm doing in my new position, and
I'm nervous about asking my manager for feedback.

6
00:19.370 --> 00:23.970
I gotcha. You should really think of it as an
opportunity to hear about what you're doing well.

7
00:24.390 --> 00:27.200
Ask for both positive and
constructive feedback from him.

8
00:27.970 --> 00:30.720
Why are you having a difficult time
connecting with your coworkers?

9
00:31.240 --> 00:33.600
I don't feel like I have much to connect on.

10
00:33.600 --> 00:37.730
Everyone's a college grad and they've done
internships at all of these cool places.

11
00:38.210 --> 00:39.750
I get how that can be uncomfortable,

12
00:40.100 --> 00:43.140
but they'd be really interested to hear
a different kind of story to theirs.

13
00:43.590 --> 00:48.070
Opening up will help you make stronger connections
here, and I'm sure your colleagues will surprise you too.

14
00:49.730 --> 00:51.490
Is there anything else that is bothering you?

15
00:52.100 --> 00:56.580
Yeah. I'm wondering why my manager
did not respond to one of my messages.

16
00:56.970 --> 01:01.410
I was trying to be more open to him about some
of my ideas, but he didn't even respond.

17
01:02.020 --> 01:05.220
Do you mind if I look over the message?
I can help and see what is going on.

18
01:05.800 --> 01:06.800
Sure.

19
01:06.980 --> 01:08.510
I can see what might have happened.

20
01:08.900 --> 01:11.010
It's kind of hard to follow since it's so long.

21
01:11.590 --> 01:15.140
Your manager probably needs some time to figure
out what the message and next steps are.

22
01:15.650 --> 01:20.190
Well, I really wanted to talk about the information
I got from Materials & Company, our supplier.

23
01:20.680 --> 01:25.500
They were telling me about all the benefits of stretch
aluminum, like the price, and that it's really thin.

24
01:25.500 --> 01:29.220
That's the problem. I hear your excitement,
but not the actual message.

25
01:29.640 --> 01:34.950
Here's how I'd restructure the message so that your manager
and I would be able to take action on this really great idea.

26
01:35.530 --> 01:37.600
This is great feedback. I really appreciate it.

27
01:38.340 --> 01:41.950
You have great ideas. Let's make sure
they're polished so that you shine here.
